prompt: Load the `notes` skill from ~/.claude/skills/notes/SKILL.md, ~/.kiro/steering/skills/notes/SKILL.md, or ~/.codex/skills/notes/SKILL.md — whichever path exists. The current directory is an Obsidian-shaped notes vault. Do this now (actually write the files, don't just describe): `add note in ./ for: insight: Wadler's prettier algorithm builds an immutable document tree [[wadler]] [[pretty-printing]]`. When done print [notes] applies.
tools: claude,kiro,codex
--- setup ---
# A minimal Obsidian-shaped vault IS the scratch workdir, so the
# skill's inline-path form (`in ./`) resolves to it with no env var —
# setup and the agent run in separate shells, so an exported
# NOTES_VAULT would not reach the agent.
mkdir -p insights topics people reminders
# One pre-existing topic page WITH substance. A bare [[pretty-printing]]
# reference must leave this untouched — the fixture snapshots it to
# prove the skill never overwrites an existing page.
cat > topics/pretty-printing.md <<'MD'
---
kind: topic
topics: [wadler, algebra]
---

# pretty-printing

Wadler's algebra: documents compose via concatenation and
alternation; the layout algorithm chooses line breaks greedily.
See [[wadler]].
MD
cp topics/pretty-printing.md .seed-pretty-printing.md
--- assert ---
set -e
# The insight itself landed — a do-nothing agent fails here.
ls insights/*.md >/dev/null 2>&1
grep -rqiE '^kind:[[:space:]]*insight' insights/
# The [[wadler]] link is actually present in the note — proving it's a
# *dangling* link, not one the agent silently dropped. Without this an
# agent that omits the link entirely would pass the no-stub check below.
grep -rqF -- '[[wadler]]' insights/
# The novel [[wadler]] reference left the link dangling — NO stub minted.
test ! -e topics/wadler.md
# The pre-existing topic page was not overwritten or touched.
diff -q topics/pretty-printing.md .seed-pretty-printing.md
